# Cheatsheet

A one-page reference for Bondy's storage stack — `bondy_db`,
`bondy_oplog`, and `bondy_mst`. The architecture chapters (see the
sidebar) are the narrative version.

## Tables (bondy_db)
{: .col-2}

### Open a DB and a table

```erlang
{ok, Db} = bondy_db:open(my_db, #{
    topology => bondy_db_topology_shared_shards
}),
{ok, T} = bondy_db:open_table(Db, users, #{
    fold_module => lww_register,   %% required: the CRDT type label
    shard_count => 8
}).
```

### Ephemeral, fused, in-memory WAL

```erlang
{ok, T} = bondy_db:open_table(Db, registry, #{
    fold_module => lww_register,        %% required
    projection_backend => ets,          %% table-level
    fused => true,                      %% table-level
    oplog_instance_opts => #{           %% instance-level knobs:
        backend => ets,                 %%   in-memory MST store
        wal_backend => mem,             %%   in-memory WAL
        durability => ephemeral         %%   ack no durable storage
    }
}).
```

### Read / write

```erlang
{ok, {Value, Hlc}} = bondy_db:read(T, Realm, Key),
ok = bondy_db:apply(T, Realm, Key, Op),
ok = bondy_db:counter_inc(Counters, Realm, Key, +1).

%% pack many Map/set commands into ONE atomic event:
ok = bondy_db:apply_batch(T, Realm, Key, [{put, F1, V1}, {rmv, F2}]),
ok = bondy_db:map_update(T, Realm, Key, #{put => #{F1 => V1}, rmv => [F2]}).
```

The op shape is CRDT-specific (e.g. `{set, Hlc, V}` for
`lww_register`, `{inc, N}` for counters). Batched writes
(`apply_batch/4` / `map_update/4`) pack many Map/set commands into one
event (one WAL/MST entry, applied atomically); not available for
counters/registers (`{error, {not_batchable, _}}`).

### Secondary indexes

```erlang
{ok, T} = bondy_db:open_table(Db, users, #{
    crdt_module => bondy_oplog_crdt_lww_register,
    indexes => [#{name => by_email,
                  extract => [email]}]   %% path into the value
}),
{ok, Hits} = bondy_db:index_get(T, Realm, by_email, Email, #{}),
{ok, Hits2} = bondy_db:index_range(T, Realm, by_email, Lo, Hi, #{
    max_lag => 1000, fallback => primary
}).
```

## The CRDT catalogue
{: .col-1}

| `crdt_module` (`bondy_oplog_crdt_*`) | tier | semantics |
|---|---|---|
| `lww_register` | 0 | last-writer-wins register; deterministic same-HLC tie-break |
| `g_counter` | 0 | grow-only counter |
| `pn_counter` | 0 | pos/neg counter, per-Origin Seq dedup |
| `g_set` | 0 | grow-only set |
| `two_p_set` | 0 | two-phase set; removal is permanent (no re-add) |
| `max_register` / `min_register` | 0 | monotone integer lattice |
| `mv_register` | 2 | concurrent writes surface as siblings |
| `aw_map` | 2 | add-wins map; pure remove; per-key sub-values |
| `aw_set` | 2 | add-wins set (concurrent add\|remove ⇒ add wins) |
| `rw_set` | 2 | remove-wins set (concurrent add\|remove ⇒ remove wins) |
| `ew_flag` | 2 | enable-wins flag |
| `dw_flag` | 2 | disable-wins flag |

tier_0 = scalar HLC; tier_2 = per-cell causal context (DVV).
Details: [The CRDT model](05_crdt_model.md).

## Freshness and consistency
{: .col-2}

### Bounded staleness (auth paths)

```erlang
%% ensure_fresh/2 -> ok | {stale, [Namespace]}
%% read_batch(BatchKeys, Opts); BatchKeys :: [{NS, Index, Bucket, Key}]
case bondy_oplog_core:ensure_fresh([users, grants], 1000) of
    ok           -> {ok, Result} = bondy_oplog_core:read_batch(BatchKeys, #{});
    {stale, NSs} -> too_stale   %% more than max_lag behind
end.
```

### Write barrier

```erlang
ok = bondy_oplog:await_apply(InstanceId, 5000).
```

### Change notification

```erlang
%% opt in per table: open_table(.., #{publish => true})
{ok, Ref} = bondy_oplog_core:subscribe(NS, all),
%%   {bondy_oplog_core_event,       NS, Key, Hlc, Op}  — local write
%%   {bondy_oplog_core_merge_event, NS, Key, Hlc, Op, Old}  — peer write (AE)
ok = bondy_oplog_core:unsubscribe(Ref).
```

The merge tag fires only for writes a peer made (reacted to via
anti-entropy); a node's own writes deliver the local tag. See
[bondy_db read side](03_bondy_db.md#change-notification).

## Operations
{: .col-2}

### Backup / restore (cold)

```erlang
{ok, _Manifest} = bondy_mst_admin:backup(SrcDir, BackupDir),
{ok, _}         = bondy_mst_admin:verify(BackupDir),
{ok, _}         = bondy_mst_admin:restore(BackupDir, TargetDir).
```

### Compaction & bootstrap

- Compaction runs on the `bondy_oplog_gc_scheduler` tick; the MST is
  a *window*, not a log.
- New replicas bootstrap from a checkpoint / catalogue snapshot, then
  catch the live tail via anti-entropy.
- Genesis peer: `seed => true`. Lifecycle gate:
  `pre_bootstrap → live`.

See [Compaction & bootstrap](06_compaction_and_bootstrap.md).

### Write→readable latency

Per-instance telemetry: how long a user write takes to become readable
in the projection (all backends). Sampled on the synchronous write path
(near-zero cost); emitted each window.

```erlang
%% [bondy_oplog, instance, write_latency]
%%   measurements: count, mean_us, p50_us, p95_us, p99_us, max_us
%%   metadata:     instance_id, interval_ms

%% config (defaults shown)
{oplog_latency, #{
    enabled => true,
    interval_ms => 10000,
    probe => #{enabled => false}   %% idle-instance heartbeat
}}.

ok = bondy_oplog_latency:set_enabled(true).
ok = bondy_oplog_latency:set_probe_enabled(true).  %% opt-in idle probe
```

Local-origin only. See [the applier chapter](04_applier.md#writereadable-latency-telemetry).
